The conversion efficiency on single section reached 11.3% (SEM, 1.0%) of all the EGFP-labeled cells in the striatum and 10.7% (SEM, 0.5%) in the cortex (radius = 300 μm) (Fig.
1c
).

Additionally, no apparent cell apoptosis was found at 1, 2, and 8 wpi (Supplementary Fig.
S5a
).

Using whole-cell patch-clamp, we observed that the converted neurons on day 10 were capable of firing repetitive spontaneous APs and evoked APs (Fig.
1l, m
).

The conversion efficiency in a single section reached 15.7% ± 1.8% of all the tdTomato-labeled cells (Fig.
4f
).

Behavioral assessment indicated a partial improvement in sensorimotor performance in ICH mice at 8–12 weeks after reprogramming (Fig.
5f–h
).

From January 24 to October 17, 2018, 15 patients with mild to moderate hearing loss were enroled in the Phase I trial at the UK site (Fig.
1
); 3 patients received 3 intratympanic doses of 25 µg LY3056480, 6 received 3 doses of 125 µg, and 3 and 3 patients received 3 doses of 200 µg and 250 µg, respectively.

The average C-peptide release in the experimental group was 1.6 ng/μg DNA (stimulation index [SI] 2.4), which is within the range reported for research-grade islets (
18
).
